# Static analysis gate. Run it with `composer analyse`; CI runs it in the Lint
# workflow, whole-tree, with no baseline.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why level 0 and not level 8
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The migration plan asks for level 8. That is the right destination and this is
# not it yet, for one concrete reason: larastan/larastan is not installed, and
# without it PHPStan has no idea what Eloquent and the facades are. Measured on
# this tree (app, bootstrap, database, routes):
#
#     level  0 →    26 errors        level  6 →  2015
#     level  1 →   481               level  7 →  2065
#     level  2 →   909               level  8 →  2068
#     level  3 →   934               level  9 →  2376
#     level  4 →   938               level 10 →  4380
#     level  5 →   956
#
# The jump from 26 to 481 is not the codebase getting worse between those two
# levels. At level 2, 802 of the 909 errors are two identifiers —
# `property.notFound` (`Access to an undefined property App\Models\Order::$id`)
# and `staticMethod.notFound` (`Call to an undefined static method
# App\Models\Product::where()`). Those are Eloquent working exactly as designed.
# Larastan exists to teach PHPStan about them and we cannot install it here.
#
# Baselining ~2000 of those to claim level 8 would not be a record of debt, it
# would be a way of not looking: the real findings would be buried among the
# magic, and nobody would ever read the file. So the gate lands where the tool
# is telling the truth, with nothing hidden behind it.
#
# Level 0 is not a token gesture. Its 26 findings on day one were, almost to a
# line, real: a relation pointing at a model that had been renamed, three
# classes constructing services and models that do not exist, a notification
# instantiating a framework class deleted in Laravel 9, and five PHP 8.4
# implicit-nullable deprecations. All fixed in the commit that added this file,
# which is why the count here is zero.
#
# To climb: install larastan/larastan (needs Composer network), add its
# extension.neon to `includes`, re-measure, and raise `level` to the highest
# rung that is clean or carries a baseline small enough that someone would
# actually read it.
parameters:
    level: 0

    # The directories ArchitectureTest calls "code that ships and runs in
    # production", and for the same reason. config/ is excluded because it is
    # array literals with nothing to infer; tests/ is excluded because without
    # larastan the Laravel test traits generate the same magic-noise as the app
    # code does, and a gate whose failures are mostly noise gets ignored.
    # Both are candidates for inclusion once larastan lands.
    paths:
        - app
        - bootstrap
        - database
        - routes

    # Match the sibling repositories: trust the code over its docblocks when the
    # two disagree, rather than reporting the docblock as certain fact.
    treatPhpDocTypesAsCertain: false

    ignoreErrors:
        # Artisan::command() binds its closure to the Command instance, so $this
        # is defined at runtime. PHPStan cannot see a runtime bindTo, and
        # larastan would not help. Scoped to this one message in this one file
        # so a genuinely undefined variable in routes/console.php still fails.
        -
            message: '#^Undefined variable: \$this$#'
            path: routes/console.php
